{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Getting the Job You Want", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "We All Have to Pay Our Bills", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 2, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 9, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Third Conditional", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "There are four types of conditional sentences in English:<ol><li>Zero Conditional - used to talk about certainty and facts</li><li>First Conditional - used to talk about real possibilities in the present or future</li><li>Second Conditional - used to talk about <span class=\"italic\">unreal</span> possibilities in the present or future</li><li>Third Conditional - used to talk about unreal <span class=\"italic\">past</span> situations</li></ol>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use the third conditional to talk about unreal situations in the past. <br/>These are things that did not happen in the past. You often use the third conditional to talk about regrets.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at the chart below for the structure of the third conditional:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Conditional Name</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Structure</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Example</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Third \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If</span> + Past Perfect, <span class=\\\"italic\\\">could</span>/<span class=\\\"italic\\\">would have</span> + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If there <span class=\\\"strong\\\">hadn't been</span> a strike, I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">would have stayed</span>.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "If management hadn't hired scab employees, I wouldn't have left. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Deep down though, I knew if they had paid me more, I'd still be there.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I would not have quit if I loved the job even a tiny bit more.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Tag Questions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">tag questions</span> to ask for clarification and confirmation.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Question tags</span> are short questions you add at the end of comments.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "They are mostly used in spoken English when you want to:<ul><li><span class=\"strong\">clarify/confirm if something is true or not true</span>, or</li><li><span class=\"strong\">to encourage a response</span> from the person you are speaking to.</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ol><li value=\"1\">An <span class=\"strong\">affirmative</span> statement is followed by a <span class=\"strong\">negative</span> question tag.<br/> Use this when you think the other person will agree by saying 'yes' <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>You <span class=\"strong\">were</span> taken by surprise, <span class=\"strong\">weren't you?</span></li> <li>You <span class=\"strong\">are</span> Canadian, <span class=\"strong\">aren't</span> you?</li> <li>She <span class=\"strong\">has</span> a brother, <span class=\"strong\">doesn't</span> she?</li> <li>He <span class=\"strong\">can</span> speak English, <span class=\"strong\">can't</span> he?</li></ul></span></li></ol>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ol><li value=\"2\">A <span class=\"strong\">negative</span> statement is followed by an <span class=\"strong\">affirmative</span> question tag.<br/> Use this when you think the other person will agree by saying  'no'  <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>You <span class=\"strong\">weren't</span> taken by surprise, <span class=\"strong\">were you? </span></li> <li>You <span class=\"strong\">aren't</span> Canadian, <span class=\"strong\">are</span> you?</li> <li>She <span class=\"strong\">doesn't</span> have a brother, <span class=\"strong\">does</span> she?</li> <li>He <span class=\"strong\">can't</span> speak English, <span class=\"strong\">can</span> he?</li></ul></span> </li></ol>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If the main verb is <span class=\"italic\">to be</span> or a <span class=\"strong\">modal verb</span>, the tag will be the same. <br/>For <span class=\"strong\">all other main verbs</span>, use the tag <span class=\"italic\">do</span>/<span class=\"italic\">does </span>or <span class=\"italic\">did</span>/<span class=\"italic\">didn't</span>. <br/>Look at the examples in the chart.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":11,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Main Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Tag\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He is/was\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"isn't/wasn't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You are\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"aren't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He can\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"can't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We could\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"couldn't we?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You will\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"won't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She has/had\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"doesn't/didn't she?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"don't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He likes\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"doesn't he?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You like\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"don't you?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You liked\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"didn't you?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "\u201cIt makes you money, doesn't it?\u201d", "type": "example"}, {"content": " \u201cNo? Then, it makes you happy, doesn't it?\u201d", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I need to dig a little deeper, don't I?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "There is opportunity in online learning, isn't there?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Talk about a funny job hunting experience, make one up or talk about a friend's or family member's experience.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write down what happened in point form.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Now, rewrite the story using hypothetical situations in the past focusing on the things you could have done differently.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Exchange stories with a partner and check each other's grammar.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Change partners and read your story.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write about a funny experience looking for a job.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use hypothetical situations in the past to retell the story.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I edit my partner's story.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my story about a funny experiences looking for a job with others.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "boils down to", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to reduce to its essential parts", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: His philosophy on work boils down to two questions: does it make you money, or does it make you happy?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob02aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use when making a job hunting strategy.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "drives me crazy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "exasperate someone", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: What big problem is driving me crazy right now?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob02aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "get your foot in the door", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to enter a business at a low level and take the opportunity to  be successful ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You just need to find a way to get your foot in the door and show them how eager you are to work there.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob02aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "piqued my interest", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to arouse interest", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It would have piqued your interest and your passion to work there.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob02aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "deep down", "type": "name"}, {"content": "you are certain that is true", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Deep down though, I knew if they had paid me more, I'd still be there.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob02aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "obsolete", "type": "name"}, {"content": "no longer in general use", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The education system is obsolete and there is opportunity in online learning, isn't there?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob02aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "eager", "type": "name"}, {"content": "show interest", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You just need to find a way to get your foot in the door and show them how eager you are to work there.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob02aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob02re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"id": 0, "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about emotions, opinions and behavior in a work situation.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about hypothetical situations in the past.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can ask for clarification and ask for someone's opinion.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " Have you ever had to look for a job?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " What strategies did you use to find one? Which were the most effective?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Searching for the perfect job.", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "questions": []}, {"id": 1, "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [1], "_data": [{"type": "instruct